Idea credit
-----------
visurail follows the format of Visual Transportation Science
(https://visualtransportationscience.org/): pairing transportation research with
interactive visualizations. visurail applies that format to rail science. No code or
content from that site is included.

Third-party works visualized (not covered by the Apache License)
------------------------------------------------------------------
Each visualization is an independent, simplified re-implementation of an idea from a
paper published under a Creative Commons Attribution (CC BY) licence. The papers are
cited on each page and in assets/js/entries.js. No code from the authors' repositories
is included. In particular, TimetableNetworkTool (GPL-3.0) is linked, not copied.

  - Lamanna, Prisma & Medeossi (2025), PLOS ONE 20(7): e0328681, CC BY 4.0
  - Pozzobon Borin, de Souza Sant'Ana, Raheel & Mahmood (2026), arXiv:2601.16592, CC BY 4.0
  - Dobruszkes (2025), EJTIR 25(1): 160–177, CC BY 4.0

